  </p>

  <h2 id="adjacent">Better-fit neighbours, if you love visuals but need a steadier base</h2>

  <p>
    Two neighbours may suit some people better, and we name them only where the reason is real.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Video and motion for brands.</strong> If you like moving pictures and clients ask for video as often as photos, video can raise the value of each booking. Start with the <a href="/blog/career-options/is-video-editing-a-good-career/">video editing verdict</a> to see its own crowding and AI risks.</li>
    <li><strong>Brand content and marketing roles.</strong> If you want a salary while you build skills, a content or marketing role where you shoot and edit for one brand gives steady pay and client lessons. Our judgement: many people use this to fund a studio later.</li>
  </ul>

